# Vauxhall Velox and Cresta PA saloon, 1957-1962.
#
# The PA: the transatlantic-styled Velox and Cresta with the wraparound
# windscreen and the tail fins, on sale for the 1958 model year after the
# London Motor Show of October 1957. The Cresta was the trimmed Velox.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_Cresta
#
# Dimensions: Cresta 4,547 x 1,740 x 1,448 mm, wheelbase 2,667 mm; the Velox
# is 4,508 mm long with no height stated. The Cresta figures are modelled
# because they are complete.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side profile; the flank is traced
# from it.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no period Vauxhall colour list was found. Black, Grey,
# Blue and Green are plain period names. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 135 km/h. Comfort 50/405, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 50. Classes 2,3.
# Dates: intro January 1958; retires staggered 1973-1976 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-velox-cresta-pa.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-velox-cresta-pa.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-velox-cresta-pa/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: one shared saloon at Cresta dimensions, with no separate
# 4.508 m Velox shell. The later one-piece rear screen and solid fins are
# modelled, and a single paint is used rather than the photographed two-tone
# finish of the Cresta.


obj=citycar
name=VauxhallVeloxCrestaPA(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=1958
intro_month=1
retire_year=1976
retire_month=6
speed=135
length=3
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=50
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=405

